<title>PAKISTAN: PIA gets flying rights to Johannesburg.</title>
<headline>PIA gets flying rights to Johannesburg.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-owned Pakistan International Airlines (PIA) is now allowed to operate three weekly flights between Karachi and Johannesburg in South Africa via the Kenyan capital Nairobi, the official APP news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said the traffic rights were agreed on Tuesday after two days of talks between Pakistani and Kenyan aviation officials.</p>
<p>Pakistan civil aviation sources said the agreement would open up new avenues for the PIA and greatly help tourists and business travellers between Pakistan and South Africa.</p>
</text>
